    "design_notes": "From the screenshots I kept the near-black green phosphor field, mint-green uppercase headings, wide-tracked monospace type, the hairline row rules and the exact eight-column SURVEILLANCE / ENGAGEMENT header (TRK, IDENT, TYPE, AZ, RNG, ALT, SPD, TTI) with units annotated, letting that table dominate the layout. From the profile I drove the identification legend from the four stated states with their friendly/neutral/caution/hostile tones (rather than the three IDENT values visible in the shot), the 8–100 km envelope and two-channel limit in the status strip and side panels, and a four-step decision strip (select, identify, assign, commit) with a deep decision slot sized for four controls plus an authority prompt. Deliberately omitted: any vendor or unit identifiers, and any control for correlation or TTI since the profile marks those automatic; they appear only as read-only AUTO indicators.",
